  "question": {
    "text": "Amongst the following, which should have the highest rms speed at the same temperature?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{H}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ rms velocity $(v_{rms}) \\propto \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{M}}$. Thus, smaller the mass, more will be the rms speed. $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ has minimum molar mass, So it has highest value of rms speed."
  }
}